																		A Simple Bar
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/spaser" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6075115); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6075115&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609857086" alt="Spaser" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6075115)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/spaser" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6075115); return false;" >Spaser</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609777606 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jan 2021 16:26</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4862026">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Mystery/Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Interview logs and also a log about when the bar manifested and when the Foundation sent an MTF in to determine if the place is a threat</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A &quot;simple&quot; bar and owner of said bar, that has the ability to hop across dimensions in order to serve as many customers as possible. Said bar<br />
sets up shop just outside a Foundation site in the middle of nowhere in the hopes of making more money.</p>
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The bartender and owner is relatively open and talkative about the people he's met and places he's been, but when the foundation start trying to find out<br />
some of the more personal questions about his and the bars history he starts getting more dismissive and less talkative. My idea is that the Owner used to run the place with his brother until they traveled to a dimension they weren't welcome in, with the consequence being that the brother is kept half dead, bloody, and basically soulless chained up in the back room of the bar. The owner is unable to let his brother die and let himself move on, so he pays the strange man who lives in the dimension a fee every month for him to help keep his brother alive. In an attempt to make as much money as he can to pay the strangers increasing demands he puts his bar down next to a very busy Foundation site. The interviews with foundation staff start fine with the owner happily telling stories and chatting, but each interview he gets more and more reserved and disturbed with hints and clues as to his brothers fate, until just before an interview the owner comes out from the backroom with blood on his hands with tears in his eyes.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> What I'm trying to go for is it starting all happy with stories and fun banter and slowly see it turn into horror.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I plan on leaving most of the history of the place only hinted at so the reader could speculate and come to their own conclusions.</p>

							</div>

								
					
